"The Code in the Corridor" is an audiovisual live coding performance that merges synthetic sounds, drum samples, and the real-time processing of live external input, capturing organic sounds and noises. Using Coypu, (Turbo)Phausto, and Bloc, the performance weaves together algorithmic composition and acousmatic improvisation. It explores the transformative potential of electronic music, reflecting on what happens when code intersects with waveforms to create a dynamic and evolving sonic experience.
